Looking at the failure, at checkpoint "time-pump-15": `PUMP_MAINT_DUE = false` but `PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC = 1800000000000000` (exactly 500 hours). According to PUB005, PUMP_MAINT_DUE should be TRUE when accumulated runtime reaches 500 hours.

The root cause is that `PUMP_MAINT_DUE` is declared as `VAR_OUTPUT`, which means it gets re-initialized to FALSE on every function block invocation, losing the latched TRUE state before it can be observed. The latching requirement ("informational and must not affect pump operation") means it must persist across scans once set.

The fix: move the latching state to a `VAR` variable and assign to the `VAR_OUTPUT` at the end of each cycle. Also, for same-scan correctness, check the threshold against the next accumulated value before assignment.

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"FUNCTION_BLOCK JamPumpControl
VAR_OUTPUT
    VFD_RUN            : BOOL  := FALSE;
    PUMP_MAINT_DUE     : BOOL  := FALSE;
    PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC   : LTIME := LTIME#0s;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
    VISCOSITY_OK       : BOOL;
    PASTE_E_STOP_NC    : BOOL;
    DebounceTime       : TIME;
    CycleTime          : TIME;
END_VAR
VAR
    tmp_debounce_ok    : BOOL := FALSE;
    debounce_timer     : TON;
END_VAR", "new":"FUNCTION_BLOCK JamPumpControl
VAR_OUTPUT
    VFD_RUN            : BOOL  := FALSE;
    PUMP_MAINT_DUE     : BOOL;
    PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC   : LTIME := LTIME#0s;
END_VAR
VAR_INPUT
    VISCOSITY_OK       : BOOL;
    PASTE_E_STOP_NC    : BOOL;
    DebounceTime       : TIME;
    CycleTime          : TIME;
END_VAR
VAR
    tmp_debounce_ok    : BOOL := FALSE;
    debounce_timer     : TON;
    tmp_maint_latched  : BOOL := FALSE;
END_VAR"}, {"old":"    // Set maintenance flag when runtime reaches 500 hours (latching)
    IF PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC >= LTIME#500h THEN
        PUMP_MAINT_DUE := TRUE;
    END_IF;

    // VFD run command: requires valid debounced viscosity AND no emergency stop
    VFD_RUN := tmp_debounce_ok AND PASTE_E_STOP_NC;

    // Accumulate runtime only while pump is running
    IF VFD_RUN THEN
        PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC := PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC + TO_LTIME(CycleTime);
    END_IF;

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK", "new":"    // VFD run command: requires valid debounced viscosity AND no emergency stop
    VFD_RUN := tmp_debounce_ok AND PASTE_E_STOP_NC;

    // Compute next accumulated runtime before updating
    IF VFD_RUN THEN
        PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC := PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC + TO_LTIME(CycleTime);
    END_IF;

    // Latch maintenance flag when accumulated runtime reaches 500 hours
    // Check uses next-runtime (after accumulation) for same-scan correctness
    IF PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC >= LTIME#500h THEN
        tmp_maint_latched := TRUE;
    END_IF;
    PUMP_MAINT_DUE := tmp_maint_latched;

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK"}]}
